      "id": "a7na3ic",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6.1 Historical Periods of Hindi Literature"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Hindi literature is categorized into major historical periods, including Bhakti Kaal and the Modern Period.",
        "The Chhayavad movement represents the Shadow or Romantic Mysticism phase in Hindi literature from 1920 to 1936.",
        "The Modern Period consists of prominent literary phases, notably the Bhartendu Era and Dwivedi Era.",
        "Jnanpith Award winners represent the most prestigious recognition in Hindi literary accomplishments."
      ],
      "id": "mk75cst"
    },
